      <p>Gold surged from ~$278 to a then-record <strong>$1,888.70</strong> over nine years. This drove a near-uninterrupted bull run with only modest drawdowns, fueled by dollar weakness, post-9/11 geopolitical risk, the GFC, and quantitative easing.</p>
